          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Abraham:</strong> We have all seen and heard references to the Dark Web on TV and in the movies and have an idea of what it is. This is where all those cyber criminals hang out, sell their tools and offer their services. But this criminal underground involves a lot more. The Dark Web isn't indexed by search engines but can be accessed by those who wish to use a special browser and almost anything that has a link to criminal enterprise can be found there.</p>
<p>Navigating it isn't easy as it is chaotic as everyone is anonymous and scammers often move around so as to avoid their victims. The Dark Web has flourished because of 'bitcoin' this crypto currency enables parties to conduct transactions anonymously. Nearly all sites conduct transactions using bitcoin, but the nature of the Dark Web means that it's not always safe to do business there, after all the place is full of scammers and criminals and we all know there is no honour amongst thieves.</p>
<p>But saying that the Dark Web is not all about illegal activities it offers opportunities for journalists and whistle-blowers to air their views and is monitored by mainstream media organisations. It also offers space for individuals from less open societies to access and have a voice in an anonymous environment.</p>
<p><strong>Nicole:</strong> The opportunities for using cloud services are there for everyone from large companies and organisations to you and I. Cloud services host software such as Adobe Creative Cloud and offer subscriptions for anyone who wishes to use their services. No longer do individuals have to buy expensive software that they may not use very often, that has to be updated or replaced when out of date. Whilst they’re subscribed all software is regularly automatically updated and therefore less likely to have security issues it is also often bundles so as to make it more cost effective. Individuals can keep their data and photographs using cloud storage which may be provided by their internet provider and have them accessible on any device, any place and at any time. Cloud gaming also opens up the world of gaming making it easier to access a wider range of new and old games without having to purchase a hard copy or download a copy, but with this the speed of the internet can have an impact.</p>
<p><strong>Abraham:</strong> Something we don't always think of as cyber crime is 'fake news' and video. We are noticing more regularly the term 'fake news' and we have all seen adds and so-called videos of famous people endorsing products and services which have nothing to do with them. Some people think that everything they see especially on the internet must be real, but we are getting more used to seeing how creative and clever individuals and groups are at tricking us into believing things.</p>
<p>Fake news is false or misleading information and can mask itself as real and when enough people believe it and it enters the public domain it can often be seen as 'real'. There have been many examples of this recently with regards to vaccines and 5G. Fake news can even affect elections and create unrest nationally and internationally.</p>
<p><strong>Nicole:</strong> Deepfakes can be more worrying, as we say 'seeing is believing' however technology has advanced so much that often what we see, should not be believed. Deep learning technology uses neural net simulation to create 'fake' video which can even bring dead people back to life and acting in today’s movies. Artificial intelligence learns what a source face looks like from different angles and then can transpose it onto a target usually another actor. Hollywood has done this in movies such as 'Rogue One' however, new software tools have made this available to all. It can be used for fun and for training videos, but it can also be used for gain and for criminal enterprise convincing people that celebrities are endorsing a product. I can also be used to discredit people using impersonators to create voiceovers. The potential for creatives and the film industry is immense but so is the potential for criminal enterprise.</p>
<p><strong>Abraham:</strong> So, there are many things that have the potential to be affected by cyber crime but one new advancement is the use of the technology of drones. Drone jacking is the way cyber criminals use toy-like drones to take control of personal information. Drones have become an important tool for farmers, photographers and videographers and law enforcement and delivery services. Drone jackers can hack drones and take control, but they can also use drones to attack others. They can cause chaos at airports, and they can use this technology for criminal enterprise such as delivering drugs to prisons, espionage and worst of all terrorism.</p>
<p>So, we can see that cyber security is an ever-changing field and can affect us all directly and indirectly. It is something that we all must be aware of and cyber security professionals need to try to keep ahead of the criminals and anticipate where they might strike next.</p>

          </toggle-section>
        
      
          
